ithub.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'm not sure if this is the best fix for the issue.\r\nIt seems like `get_persistent_signal_connection_count` is used to determine if a signal was actually disconnected.\r\n\r\nA different solution might be to return a boolean from `Object::disconnect` which informs whether a disconnect happened. It seems like `Object::disconnect` is calling `_disconnect`, which _does_ return a bool. While it is not documented what the bool does, it seems like it might fit the bill.\r\nIf `disconnect` was made to return that bool, and further uresd for the update check instead of calling `get_persistent_signal_connection_count`, it may be possible to eliminate unnecessary lookups, reducing the lookup speed further without introducing new optimization logic.","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109517#pullrequestreview-3109279563","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109517","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109517#pullrequestreview-3109279563"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109517"}},"submitted_at":"2025-08-12T08:39:05Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3114392344,"node_id":"PRR_kwDO